    "doi": null,
    "abstract": "To answer the questions of whether global warming is accelerating and when the 1.5\u00b0C Paris Agreement target will be exceeded, the global mean surface temperature from 1880 to 2025 is first examined using a purely graphical approach and later, in a more conventional way, using various time-domain and frequency-domain methods. In an effort to reduce variability, exogenous variables such as El Ni\u00f1o and solar variations are taken into account. Although it ultimately remains unclear to what extent these variables are actually helpful, we feel confident in summarizing the empirical results of this study to suggest that global warming is indeed accelerating and that a breach of the 1.5\u00b0C Paris Agreement target is imminent. But when it comes to statistical significance, caution should still be exercised. While the acceleration hypothesis can be confirmed with a fair degree of certainty under reasonably plausible assumptions (albeit with the help of a bit of data snooping, which is unavoidable when building on the results of earlier studies that used virtually the same data), there is currently not enough evidence to prove that the 1.5\u00b0C target has already been exceeded. However, if 2026 and 2027 turn out to be very warm due to the approaching El Ni\u00f1o, that could change very soon.",
    "field": "Statistical analysis of global warming",
    "problem": "Existing statistical methods struggle to robustly detect the acceleration of global warming and the imminent 1.5\u00b0C breach, as complex models require questionable assumptions and risk data snooping, while simpler approaches are often biased, creating uncertainty.",
    "method": "The paper proposes a combined graphical and statistical time series analysis of global temperature data, accounting for exogenous variables, to determine if warming is accelerating and when the 1.5\u00b0C Paris Agreement target will be breached.",
    "task": "The task is to determine whether global warming is accelerating and when the 1.5\u00b0C Paris Agreement target will be exceeded by examining global mean surface temperature data from 1880 to 2025 using various graphical and statistical methods.",
